Allow large 2D framebuffer backing attachments alongside pending commands.
A 5120x2880 32-bit framebuffer has 14,400 4 KiB pages. With one memory
entry per page, its attachment needs 57 entry-list descriptors plus the
request and response: 59 descriptors. A 64-entry control queue cannot
hold that request with even three other two-descriptor commands pending.
Match the existing 3D queue capacity; leave cursor queues unchanged.

This increases the migratable device's maximum queue size. State saved
with a queue larger than 64 cannot be loaded by the older 64-entry build.

--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@
         virtio_add_queue(vdev, 256, ctrl_cb);
         virtio_add_queue(vdev, 16, cursor_cb);
     } else {
-        virtio_add_queue(vdev, 64, ctrl_cb);
+        virtio_add_queue(vdev, 256, ctrl_cb);
         virtio_add_queue(vdev, 16, cursor_cb);
     }
 
